{"skill":"codex","type":"pitfall","key":"app-release-cannot-depend-on-app-test","insight":"In workroom, `make app-release` must NOT depend on `app-test`. app-test builds Debug, and Debug pins CODE_SIGN_STYLE: Automatic + CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY: \"Apple Development\" (macapp/project.yml). release.yml and nightly.yml import a Developer ID cert ONLY and pass no APP_SIGN_FLAGS, so the prerequisite fails provisioning on a fresh runner before anything is archived. ci.yml gets away with `make app-test` because it passes ad-hoc overrides. Gate the release with a separate workflow STEP carrying those same overrides, placed BEFORE the release step.","confidence":9,"source":"cross-model","files":["Makefile",".github/workflows/nightly.yml",".github/workflows/release.yml"],"ts":"2026-08-09T14:02:10.963Z","trusted":false}
{"skill":"review","type":"pitfall","key":"weak-self-skips-shared-counter-release","insight":"In workroom macapp, any per-window object (AppStore, RemoteStateModel) that increments a counter on the SHARED ProjectStore before an async Task, then decrements it via guard let self else return or self? inside that Task, leaks the counter forever if the window closes mid-operation - ProjectStore outlives the window, so nothing else ever releases it. Fixed for writingProjectRoots/committingProjectRoots by capturing projectStore (not self) strongly at Task-launch time and releasing through a static helper (AppStore.releaseWrite) that takes ProjectStore explicitly. Any FUTURE per-project in-flight counter on ProjectStore needs the same pattern from day one, not bolted on after a leak is found.","confidence":9,"source":"observed","files":["macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/AppStore+WorkroomStatus.swift","macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/RemoteStateModel.swift","macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/AppStore.swift"],"ts":"2026-08-10T13:20:39.684Z","trusted":false}

